From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:55:28 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS] Fix use-after-free in libxslt direct pattern match cache

xsltTestCompMatchDirect read the cached node-set from the transform
context's runtime extras before calling xmlXPathEval, then freed that
pointer afterwards. The evaluation can re-enter the function for the
same cache slot (e.g. via a lazily evaluated global variable whose value
runs xsl:number), and the nested call may free and replace the cached
object, resulting in a double free. Re-read the slot after the
evaluation.

Fixed: 582442907, 572578603
Change-Id: I535c3ba61bfdc951683590cd31f4fc6b8fa0a46a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8762073
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Nasko Oskov <nasko@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Srinivas Sista <srinivassista@chromium.org>
